THE GARBAGE COLLECTOR IN THE RELEASED RUNTIME IS MODIFIED
---------------------------------------------------------

The mono-2.0-bdwgc.dll published with releases of this project is not Unity's runtime. It
is built from the sources above with these changes:

  - BDWGC is compiled with PARALLEL_MARK, so marking runs on several threads. BDWGC picks the
    number of marker threads from the processor count; the GC_MARKERS environment variable
    overrides it, read even though the build sets NO_GETENV. The threads are named
    "BDWGC marker".
  - GC_mark_some's parallel branch calls Unity's mark-stack-empty hook, which the unmodified
    source calls only on the serial path. Unity's ephemeron (ConditionalWeakTable) support
    depends on that hook.
  - BDWGC is compiled with USE_MARK_BITS, one mark bit per granule instead of one mark byte.
  - The runtime exports oni_gc_version(), which returns the version of this patch set.

The exact changes are patches/b3-markbits/bdwgc.patch and patches/b3-markbits/mono.patch.


